{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_mcp_llm.py","reason":"the MCP admission point: _spawn_gate_daemon starts gate work on an in-process daemon thread, so the counter must be acquired here before a run starts and released when it ends, including on the failure path"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/plan_review/__init__.py","reason":"plan-review library entry point — one of the two operations that snapshots the repo at a ref and therefore consumes the bounded resource; CLI runs reach the gate through here, not through the MCP daemon"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/completion.py","reason":"verify_completion entry point — the second consumer sharing the same counter, per the operator's decision that both operations contend for the same disk"},{"path":"src/rebar/_config_schema.py","reason":"declare the concurrency limit as a config key with a measured default; a new config key trips the shrink-only mechanism ratchet and needs an in-tree mechanism-ok marker naming this ticket"},{"path":"docs/config.md","reason":"document the key, its default and the rationale for that default, per AC6"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_gate_admission_09da.py","reason":"the oracle: limit+1 executions rejects the last; the rejection is immediate rather than blocking; the error shape is distinguishable from a gate verdict over both MCP and CLI; crash-safe slot reclamation; and metric emission on rejection"}]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"FILE_IMPACT","timestamp":1788478093421126001,"uuid":"3daef95e-9dbe-44d9-b7e7-3766db8ae34d"}